                <pb facs="0666" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00/2953: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-29T14:00:00-04:00">April 29, 1931—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Legation’s 34, April 28, 1 p.m. You are authorized to inform the Haitian
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs that the Government of the United States desires to
                    withdraw the forces of occupation at the earliest moment when it feels that it
                    can properly do so, but that it does not consider it practicable at the present
                    time to attempt to fix any definite date or program.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
